# Results and reports are provenance, not editable text.
#
# A run's "inputs digest" is a SHA-256 over the bytes of its result JSON. Git's
# line-ending conversion rewrites those bytes on checkout (on Windows, with
# core.autocrlf=true), so identical measurements hash differently after a clone, a
# new worktree or a branch switch. Pinning LF keeps a digest meaning what the
# reports say it means.
#
# Study 01 pins its own v3 runs in studies/01-charity-tree/.gitattributes, which was
# deliberately scoped so that historical runs' bytes are not rewritten without an
# audit. These rules cover studies 02 and 03, whose runs were produced with LF.
studies/02-ticket-booking/results/**/*.json text eol=lf
studies/02-ticket-booking/reports/**/*.md text eol=lf
studies/03-reserved-seating/results/**/*.json text eol=lf
studies/03-reserved-seating/reports/**/*.md text eol=lf
